        "why_best": "Random Forest (Tuned) achieved the highest overall performance (ROC-AUC: 0.9241, Accuracy: 90.91%) for three key reasons:\n1. Variance Reduction through Bagging: A single Decision Tree suffers from high variance and easily overfits noisy customer records. Random Forest trains multiple diverse trees on bootstrap samples and averages their probabilistic predictions, drastically reducing generalization error.\n2. Non-Linear Interaction Modeling: Unlike Logistic Regression, which assumes a linear boundary in log-odds space, Random Forest effortlessly captures complex non-linear combinations between features (such as cart abandonment rate interacting with customer service calls and recency).\n3. Robustness to Skew & Outliers: Tree-based ensemble splits are invariant to monotonic feature scales, making the model remarkably resilient across diverse behavioural and monetary attributes."
